After countless YASD and YAAD, and a handful of failed gehennom
attempts (notably genociding myself on the bottom level and getting
killed by a salamander while dancing with a nurse), I finally
managed to ascend last night at 5am on the public NAO server.

A seemingly unpromising start for a Gnomish wizard, kishi survived
several near-death experiences in the early game, his pets
consistently died, and he spent much time running back and forth
between stashes due to the absense of any BoH - which became
his first castle wish.  The second wish was for speed boots, then
two magic markers to fill out the AK.  In preparation for Gehennom
I spent some time to cast and #enhance up all the spellcasting
skills to at least basic.  Unfortunately, while repeatedly healing
myself with the key sequence "Zq." I slipped once and typed "zq."
q happened to be a wand of cancellation (carried fearlessly because
until a few turns previously I had no BoH).  Being cancelled isn't fun
-
everything is unblessed, the armor I had just maxed out with ?oEA
was reduced to +0, and my final two wishes were lost.

I made a hasty retreat then started altar squatting hoping for
something good to turn up.  My very next prayer got me crowned,
which slowed the whole process.  A black pudding turned up, so
I decided to try my hand at farming, which I had never done before.
The whole level was soon half full of pudding, and I realized I was
in danger.  Even after FoDing a path through the pudding, I'd take
a step and then instantly be surrounded again.  A storm giant
started wading his way through the pudding towards me, but
after getting knocked down into the red I made it back to the stairs
and was able to rest up before going back and FoDing the rest
of the mess.

After all this I still had gotten nothing but a motley collection of
useless scrolls and potions, and the Vorpal blade.  I polyed the
scrolls and potions into oblivion until I got enough ?oEA to get
my AC back down.  Weilding the Vorpal, I entered Gehennom.
Every demon except Baelzebub, Vlad, and several Jabberwocky
got decapitated.  The cat in the box was alive, tamed and two
turns later ate a chameleon corpse and became Schroedinger's
Tiger.  A little later an Umber Hulk rounded a corner with horrible
timing and the poor Tiger numbered among those to lose his
head to the Vorpal Blade.  My emergency-use 1:20 magic
marker was quickly used to get revenge on all Umber Hulks,
everywhere.

I was completely unspoiled (and unprepared) for the Astral and
it took a while, but after changing my strategy to remove conflict
and charm everything that got close (including several Archons)
I made it through.  Much thanks to GreyKnight and all those on
#nethack for the help and moral support at the end.  A last minute
c?oG at the altar got me 4 woodchuck pets, who were named after
those most active on #nethack at the time and ascended with me.

I'll take a break and leave the final game up for a while:

